architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:5:Implement Wave 007 by introducing a focused 2D rendering read-model/selector layer between the domain `World` and the canvas renderer. The selector owns domain traversal, realization lookup, style/visibility resolution, active-plane emphasis, projected-3D-on-2D inclusion, and hit-test/query geometry. Renderer adapters then convert those DTOs into `Paper` primitives and SVG attributes. `SvgCanvas.vue` becomes a composition/input shell over selectors, query adapters, and the existing Wave 006a command controllers.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:13:  ├─ injects World only as selector input / existing command-controller input
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:19:  ├─ walks World/projection planes
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:25:  └─ maps RenderItem2D DTOs to Paper primitives; no World traversal or style decisions
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:31:  └─ stores/query primitives or is reduced to pure primitive collection; no raw World hit-test dependency
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:39:  - `Canvas2DViewModel` with `renderItems`, `hitItems`, `planeTransforms`, required `gridModel`, `labelModel`, and metadata for active plane/view toggles. Grid/label extraction is in Wave 007 scope, not a deferred residual, because the scope check identifies active-plane grid realization in `SvgCanvas.vue` as a remaining raw-domain canvas read leak.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:40:  - `RenderItem2D` discriminated union for point, infinite line, finite segment, circle, guide, sibling guide, hinge line, half-hinge line, arc, projected-3D point/line/segment, grid line, and text/label if needed.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:41:  - `HitItem2D` discriminated union carrying source entity ID, selectable type, plane ID, plane-space geometry, paper-space geometry where needed, and selection-mask metadata. It must explicitly represent point, infinite-line, finite-segment, guide/sibling-guide, hinge/half-hinge, and circle query geometry rather than collapsing all line-like cases into one unbounded branch.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:42:  - `SnapPoint2D` / snap-output DTOs for the current snap-preview and construction-input behavior so snapping is derived from selector/query state rather than raw `World` access.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:47:- Add `frontend/src/application/rendering2d/PaperHitQuery.ts` to perform hit testing over `HitItem2D` DTOs rather than raw `World`/active-plane iteration. The query contract must preserve current `Paper.hitTest()` semantics for points, infinite lines, finite segments, guides, sibling guides, hinge lines, half-hinge lines, circles, active-plane filtering, selection-mask filtering, closest-element priority, and snap-point output. Segment items must use finite segment distance checks; infinite line, guide, sibling-guide, hinge, and half-hinge items must retain their current line-like pickability only where the active-plane realization currently makes them pickable.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:55:- Reduce `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` to pure primitive collection/hover state or move query behavior into `PaperHitQuery`. `Paper.hitTest()` should no longer accept `World` or realize domain objects.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:62:  - Use `PaperHitQuery` for selection, properties, hover, snap-preview, drag hit behavior, and snap-point output.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:63:  - Consume selector-produced `gridModel`/`labelModel` for active-plane grid rendering instead of realizing grid geometry in the component.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:65:  - Remove component-owned `PrimitiveContext` creation and direct `Paper.hitTest(..., world, selectionMask)` calls.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:69:- Add `frontend/tests/unit/application/rendering2d/canvas2DSelectors.spec.ts` covering selector output for points, infinite lines, finite segments, circles, guides, sibling guides, hinge lines, half-hinge lines, active-plane emphasis, selected/hovered/cascade style, visibility, z-order, projected-3D toggling, plane transforms, grid lines, and grid labels.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:70:- Add `frontend/tests/unit/application/rendering2d/paperHitQuery.spec.ts` covering hit behavior previously dependent on `Paper.hitTest()`: active-plane filtering, selection masks, point hits, infinite-line hits, finite-segment endpoint/interior/outside misses, circle hits, guide and sibling-guide hits, hinge/half-hinge line hits, snap-point output, and closest-element priority.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:82:- Delete `frontend/src/services/RenderService.ts` if static search confirms it is only used by tests. Its own comments state `renderPlane()` and `renderLine()` are test-only while production uses `SVGRenderer` (`frontend/src/services/RenderService.ts:111`, `:163`), and `renderLine()` contains test-compatibility-only `planeName` fields (`frontend/src/services/RenderService.ts:181`).
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:84:- Delete `PaperService` methods that traverse raw `World`, resolve visibility, branch on domain classes, or inspect `(line as any).arcGeometry` after equivalent selector DTO behavior exists.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:87:- Delete direct `Paper.hitTest(..., world, ...)` usage in `SvgCanvas.vue` and `Paper.ts`; do not leave a compatibility overload. If `Paper.ts` remains, it must not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or perform raw realization traversal.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:88:- Delete duplicate primitive special cases that exist only because `PaperService` mixes selector and adapter responsibilities, such as separate raw-domain guide/segment/half-hinge branches in renderer code after selector DTOs discriminate them.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:95:- Hit behavior remains equivalent for selection, hover tooltip, snap-preview, properties dialog opening, point movement, construction selection masks, active-plane filtering, and snap-point output across points, infinite lines, finite segments, circles, guides/sibling guides, and hinge/half-hinge line paths.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:104:   - Verify `RenderService.ts` is deleted, or if an implementation decision retains a named file temporarily, verify it is fully unused by production and tests before wave completion; the preferred outcome is deletion with no replacement shim.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:105:   - Verify renderer adapter modules do not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or domain realization types; raw domain imports are permitted only in selector/query modules.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:106:   - Verify `SvgCanvas.vue` has no `Paper.hitTest(... world ...)`, no `PrimitiveContext`, no direct `paperService.generatePrimitives(context)` path, and no component-owned active-plane grid realization.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:107:   - Verify `Paper.ts`, if retained, does not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or perform raw realization traversal.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:115:   - Selector tests must assert rendering DTOs for point, infinite line, finite segment, circle, guide, sibling guide, hinge/half-hinge line, projected-3D, style/visibility, active-plane emphasis, grid, labels, and plane transforms.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:116:   - Hit-query tests must assert active-plane filtering, selection masks, point/line/finite-segment/circle/guide/sibling-guide/hinge/half-hinge hits, snap-point output, closest-element priority, and misses outside finite segment extents.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:117:   - Include `tests/unit/services/renderService.spec.ts` only if rewritten as selector/adapter coverage; otherwise delete it with `RenderService.ts`.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-direct.md:137:- **Risk: hit testing changes while visual rendering passes.** Mitigate by treating hit/query DTOs as first-class selector output and adding focused `PaperHitQuery` tests before deleting old `Paper.hitTest()` behavior, including non-point/non-circle cases: finite segments, guides/sibling guides, hinge/half-hinge line paths, active-plane filtering, selection masks, and snap-point output.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:20:  ├─ CanvasPresentationSelector.ts   # raw World traversal and realization lookup
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:36:Current evidence shows several raw-domain reads are outside the `PaperService.generatePrimitives()` call:
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:39:- `SvgCanvas.vue` calls `Paper.hitTest(..., world, selectionMask)` for selection, drag, properties, hover, and snap preview (`frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:1212`-`1227`, `:1350`-`:1357`, `:1411`-`:1418`, `:1531`-`:1547`).
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:57:  - explicit discriminants for point, infinite line, finite segment, circle, guide, sibling guide, hinge line, half-hinge line, arc, and projected 3D point/line/segment. Query DTOs must not collapse finite segments into unbounded line-like geometry.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:58:- Add `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationSelector.ts` to build the model from `World` and UI state. This is the only new module allowed to branch on raw domain classes and call domain realization APIs for 2D canvas presentation.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:61:- Add `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasInteractionQuery.ts` to answer hit/snap/properties queries from `CanvasQueryItem` DTOs and selection masks. The query contract must preserve current `Paper.hitTest()` behavior for points, infinite lines, finite segments, circles, guides, sibling guides, hinge lines, half-hinge lines, active-plane filtering, selection-mask filtering, closest-element priority, and snap-point output. Segment matching must remain finite; line-like guides/hinges must remain pickable only through the active-plane realization semantics that currently make them pickable.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:66:- Replace `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts` with one or more adapter modules that map `CanvasRenderItem` to `Paper`/SVG primitives. If a compatibility adapter is temporarily needed during the same implementation, it must be deleted before the wave completes. Renderer adapters must not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or domain realization types.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:68:- Refactor `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` so it no longer imports `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or raw domain realization types, and no longer performs raw realization traversal. Either keep it as a pure primitive collection or delete it if `SvgCanvasRenderer` can render directly from canvas DTOs.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:81:- Add `frontend/tests/unit/application/canvasPresentation/canvasPresentationSelector.spec.ts` for end-to-end model construction from a test world, including render/query DTOs for points, infinite lines, finite segments, circles, guides, sibling guides, hinge/half-hinge lines, projected-3D output, style/visibility, active-plane emphasis, plane transforms, grid lines, and labels.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:82:- Add `frontend/tests/unit/application/canvasPresentation/canvasInteractionQuery.spec.ts` for selection-mask/hit/snap/properties behavior, including active-plane filtering, point hits, infinite-line hits, finite-segment endpoint/interior/outside misses, circle hits, guide/sibling-guide hits, hinge/half-hinge hits, snap-point output, and closest-element priority.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:85:- Update/delete old Paper/RenderService tests as below.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:89:- Delete `frontend/src/services/RenderService.ts` and obsolete `frontend/tests/unit/services/renderService.spec.ts` if the latter only protects the test-only production service.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:90:- Delete or radically shrink `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts`; no method that traverses `World`, calls `resolveVisibility`, realizes elements, or branches on raw domain classes should remain in a renderer adapter.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:91:- Delete `Paper.hitTest(world, ...)` from `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts`; replace with `CanvasInteractionQuery`. No compatibility overload should remain.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:93:- Delete direct canvas rendering access to raw domain internals replaced by `CanvasPresentationSelector`, including direct `world.projectionPlanes` iteration in rendering code and direct `paperService.generatePrimitives(context)` calls.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:95:- Delete duplicate render special cases that only existed because `PaperService` simultaneously identified domain kind and rendered primitives, including duplicate guide/segment/half-hinge renderer branches after canvas-presentation DTOs discriminate those cases.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:102:- Rendering, hit testing, snapping, snap-point output, properties-target lookup, style/visibility, active-plane emphasis, and grid/label output derive from one coherent selector snapshot, reducing drift between what is visible and what is selectable. Current pick semantics are preserved for points, infinite lines, finite segments, circles, guides/sibling guides, hinge/half-hinge line paths, active-plane filtering, and selection masks.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:110:   - `SvgCanvas.vue` no longer contains direct `world.projectionPlanes` rendering iteration, direct active-plane grid realization code, `PrimitiveContext`, `paperService.generatePrimitives`, or `Paper.hitTest(... world ...)`.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:111:   - Renderer adapters do not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or domain realization types; raw domain imports are permitted only in canvas-presentation selector/query modules.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:112:   - `Paper.ts`, if retained, no longer imports `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or performs raw realization traversal.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:113:   - `RenderService.ts` is deleted, or if an implementation decision temporarily retains a named file, it is proven fully unused before wave completion; the preferred outcome is deletion with no shim.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:117:   - Selector/model tests must assert DTO output for point, infinite-line, finite-segment, circle, guide, sibling-guide, hinge/half-hinge, projected-3D, style/visibility, active-plane emphasis, grid, labels, and plane transforms.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:118:   - Interaction tests must assert active-plane filtering, selection masks, point/line/finite-segment/circle/guide/sibling-guide/hinge/half-hinge hits, snap-point output, properties-target lookup, closest-element priority, and misses outside finite segment extents.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:128:- **Risk: hit/select mismatch.** Mitigate by deriving visible render items and query items from the same selector snapshot and adding focused tests that assert invisible/non-active/non-mask-matching elements are not hit, finite segments remain finite, guide/sibling-guide and hinge/half-hinge paths remain pickable where current active-plane realization allows, and snap-point output remains equivalent.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:13:**Reviewer requirement:** Preserve current semantics for points, infinite lines, finite segments, guides/sibling guides, hinge/half-hinge line paths, circles, active-plane filtering, selection-mask filtering, and snap-point output; add focused tests for these cases.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:17:- `proposals/proposal-direct.md` now requires `RenderItem2D`/`HitItem2D` discriminants for finite segments, guides, sibling guides, hinge lines, half-hinge lines, and circles instead of generic line-like collapse.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:18:- `proposals/proposal-direct.md` now defines `PaperHitQuery` parity obligations for finite segment distance checks, active-plane realization semantics for guide/hinge pickability, selection masks, closest-element priority, and snap-point output.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:19:- `proposals/proposal-direct.md` focused tests now explicitly cover finite segment endpoint/interior/outside misses, guide/sibling-guide hits, hinge/half-hinge hits, active-plane filtering, masks, and snap points.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:28:- `proposals/proposal-direct.md` now makes `gridModel` and `labelModel` required parts of `Canvas2DViewModel`, not optional residuals.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:35:**Reviewer requirement:** Add post-implementation checks for `RenderService.ts` deletion/unused state, renderer adapter import boundaries, removal of `PrimitiveContext`/`generatePrimitives`/`Paper.hitTest(world)` from `SvgCanvas.vue`, and `Paper.ts` no longer importing `World` if retained.
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:40:  - `RenderService.ts` is deleted or fully unused before wave completion, with deletion preferred;
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:41:  - renderer adapters do not import `World`, projection-plane classes, concrete domain element classes, or realization types;
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:42:  - `SvgCanvas.vue` no longer constructs `PrimitiveContext`, calls `paperService.generatePrimitives(context)`, calls `Paper.hitTest(... world ...)`, or owns grid realization;
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:43:  - `Paper.ts`, if retained, no longer imports `World` or raw domain types and performs no realization traversal;
architecture-audit/cycle-007-2d-rendering-selectors-adapters/corrections-round-01-note.md:49:The corrected set keeps Proposal Restructure as the recommended path because it matches the reviewer’s preferred higher-level read boundary for rendering, grid, hit/snap/properties, style, and visibility. Proposal Direct is also corrected enough for comparison because it now includes grid/label extraction and an explicit hit-query parity contract. Both proposals continue to avoid premature Wave 008 `ThreeView.vue` scene-adapter work and maintain the no-backcompat/delete-first priorities for `RenderService.ts`, old `Paper.hitTest(world)` behavior, obsolete rendering TODOs, duplicate render special cases, and compatibility shims.
